      <slug></slug>
      <title>Manos: web apps for the lazy hacker</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Mono devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Manos: web apps for the lazy hacker&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Web development is a world of its own and the old-school hacker within us tends to be mystified by all these Macbook people talking about weird stuff like Rails, RESTful or NodeJS.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;But have no worries, this talk is for you (who always thought web development wasn&amp;#39;t your cup of tea) and it will walk you through the steps of building a web application using Manos, the easy to use, high performance web application framework that stays out of your way and makes your life ridiculously simple.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Forget about MVC, forget about ASP.NET, we are here to bring the fun of hacking into web development.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2051">Jérémie Laval</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>